<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/mykrok> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "MyKrok (Ukrainian: \"мій крок\" — \"my step\") is a CLI tool to incrementally back up fitness activities from Strava, including GPS tracks, photos, comments, and kudos. Backups are browsable offline through a built-in web frontend with interactive maps and activity statistics — applying the same git-annex / open-data philosophy of CON's archival tools to personal fitness data. Try the live demo with synthetic data." .
