_:rae80c039cd6d4604b4b09707_n2b12c63e071047b0aa35bf06ce091b9cb1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"https://github.com/con/annextube\">con/annextube</a> is a YouTube-channel archiving system that uses <a href=\"http://git-annex.branchable.com\">git-annex</a> for efficient, incremental storage of videos, metadata, comments, and captions. Archives are browsable offline through a client-side web interface generated by annextube itself. Actively maintained archives include: </p> <ul> <li> <a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/centerforopenneuroscience/contube/web/\">CON/tube</a> — CON's own channel archive (<a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/centerforopenneuroscience/contube\">dataset</a>) </li> <li> <a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/repronim/ReproTube/web/\">ReproTube</a> — archive covering channels from <a href=\"http://repronim.org\">ReproNim</a>, <a href=\"https://afni.nimh.nih.gov\">AFNI</a>, <a href=\"https://datalad.org\">DataLad</a>, and others (<a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/repronim/ReproTube\">dataset</a>) </li> </ul>" .
