_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"https://github.com/ReproNim/containers\">ReproNim/containers</a> is a <a href=\"#datalad\">DataLad</a> dataset providing a ready-to-use \"distribution\" of containerized neuroimaging environments (Singularity images) for reproducible analysis. It collects a curated set of containers — including those used by <a href=\"#heudiconv\">HeuDiConv</a> and the broader <a href=\"http://repronim.org\">ReproNim</a> ecosystem — and exposes them via the <code>///repronim/containers</code> DataLad dataset path, making it trivial to pin and share exact software environments alongside data and workflows. </p>" .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "ReproNim/containers" .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/anchor> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "repronim-containers" .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "ReproNim/containers is a DataLad dataset providing a ready-to-use \"distribution\" of containerized neuroimaging environments (Singularity images) for reproducible analysis. It collects a curated set of containers — including those used by HeuDiConv and the broader ReproNim ecosystem — and exposes them via the ///repronim/containers DataLad dataset path, making it trivial to pin and share exact software environments alongside data and workflows." .
_:rb8ce4759263aedf0c619b26c_na120e9a647f2428abbf45208d3552cc7b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/section> .
