_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "STAMPED is a set of seven principles, Self-containment, Tracking, Actionability, Modularity, Portability, Ephemerality, and Distributability, for building research objects that others can trust, rerun, and build upon. Each principle is a spectrum from a practical minimum to an aspirational ideal, so adoption can be incremental and start from existing practice. STAMPED grew out of YODA and comes with an interactive checklist and worked examples." .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "STAMPED Principles" .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/anchor> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "stamped" .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rcb9ad497d87096d02d26e206_nfe9e48ff3fc3482daaebb2c7e11623ecb9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"https://stamped-principles.org\">STAMPED</a> is a set of seven principles, Self-containment, Tracking, Actionability, Modularity, Portability, Ephemerality, and Distributability, for building research objects that others can trust, rerun, and build upon. Each principle is a spectrum from a practical minimum to an aspirational ideal, so adoption can be incremental and start from existing practice. STAMPED grew out of <a href=\"https://f1000research.com/posters/7-1965\">YODA</a> and comes with an <a href=\"https://checklist.stamped-principles.org\">interactive checklist</a> and <a href=\"https://examples.stamped-principles.org\">worked examples</a>. </p> <ul> <li> <a href=\"/whoweare#austin_macdonald_\" class=\"centroid\">Austin Macdonald</a>, <a href=\"/whoweare#cody_baker_\" class=\"centroid\">Cody C. Baker</a>, <a href=\"/whoweare#isaac_to_\" class=\"centroid\">Isaac To</a>, <a href=\"/whoweare#john_lee_\" class=\"centroid\">John A. Lee</a>, <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Yaroslav O. Halchenko</a>. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.31222/osf.io/f3h82_v1\">STAMPED principles for reproducible research objects</a> (preprint). DOI: 10.31222/osf.io/f3h82_v1 </li> <li> 🎬 <a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/centerforopenneuroscience/contube/web/#/video/8NTWKHer5Zo\">Talk by Cody C. Baker introducing STAMPED</a> — archived on CON/tube. </li> <li> 🎬 <a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/centerforopenneuroscience/contube/web/#/video/1XbTbJ_P2x0\">YODA: Structure your studies, observable and reproducible they become</a> — webinar recording archived on CON/tube. </li> </ul>" .
