_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Software" .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Python-based framework for neural decoding using multivariate pattern analysis. Supports volume and surface-based analyses, supervised/unsupervised learning, representational similarity analyses, searchlight analyses, hyperalignment, and model-based decoding/encoding." .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/logo_style> .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "width:395px;padding-right:10px;margin-top:0em;" .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"http://www.pymvpa.org\">PyMVPA</a> is a Python-based framework for neural decoding using multivariate pattern analysis. It affords both volume- and surface-based analyses using a wide variety of supervised and unsupervised machine learning methods, representational similarity analyses, searchlight analyses, hyperalignment of representational spaces, and model-based decoding and encoding. The software also can be used for neural data other than fMRI, including analysis of MEG and EEG data through spatio-temporo-frequency band searchlights and cross-modal EEG to fMRI trans-fusion. It also has been used for analyses on data unrelated to neuroscience, demonstrating its general utility. PyMVPA also serves as a repository for sample data sets (e.g., Haxby et al. 2001) that has found wide applicability for education, development of new algorithms, or new analyses and independent research reports. </p> <ul> <li> <a href=\"/whoweare#michael_hanke_\" class=\"centroid\">M. Hanke</a>, <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Y.O. Halchenko</a>, et al. (2009). <a href=\"http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007%2Fs12021-008-9041-y\">PyMVPA: A Python toolbox for multivariate pattern analysis of fMRI data.</a> Neuroinformatics, 7, 37-53. DOI: 10.1007/s12021-008-9041-y </li> </ul>" .
_:re64c20da4ae3d73b5e70c0af_n4f7b195d18714f63bee84ac02f0b1fc1b16 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/homepage> .
