_:re9d825308c06f8f8f7158d5f_ne43c0c4b1ff049d19b16929b5afd4245b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/Association> .
_:re9d825308c06f8f8f7158d5f_ne43c0c4b1ff049d19b16929b5afd4245b6 <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/roles> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/agent-roles/7e8c6eda-7d12-4c9f-9a3e-225e53a3db46> .
_:re9d825308c06f8f8f7158d5f_ne43c0c4b1ff049d19b16929b5afd4245b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:re9d825308c06f8f8f7158d5f_ne43c0c4b1ff049d19b16929b5afd4245b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re9d825308c06f8f8f7158d5f_ne43c0c4b1ff049d19b16929b5afd4245b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"http://bids.neuroimaging.io\">BIDS</a> is a project lead by a steering group elected by the BIDS community to provide a simple and intuitive way to organize and describe your neuroimaging and behavioral data. </p> <ul> <li> Gorgolewski, K. J., et many, <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Y.O. Halchenko</a> et many more (2016). <a href=\"http://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201644\">The brain imaging data structure, a format for organizing and describing outputs of neuroimaging experiments.</a> Scientific Data, 3. DOI: 10.1038/sdata.2016.44 </li> <li> <a href=\"https://github.com/bids-standard/bids-examples\">Example (test) datasets</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"http://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/openfmri\">Historical OpenfMRI</a> and up-to-date <a href=\"http://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/openneuro\">OpenNeuro</a> Datasets in DataLad distribution. </li> <li> <a href=\"https://github.com/bids-dandisets\">bids-dandisets</a>: a GitHub organization hosting individual DANDI dandisets converted to BIDS format using <a href=\"#nwb\">con/nwb2bids</a>, with a <a href=\"https://github.com/bids-dandisets/dashboard\">conversion dashboard</a> tracking the status across all dandisets. </li> </ul>" .
